{"id":"acc-sg","course":"declension","ord":1,"titleEn":"Accusative singular","titleSk":"Akuzatív jednotného čísla","case":"acc","number":"sg","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"acc","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.4},{"case":"acc","number":"sg","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.3},{"case":"acc","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.2},{"case":"acc","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.1}],"triggerIds":["verb-vidiet","prep-pre","prep-na-acc","q-koho-acc","q-co-acc"]},"summaryMd":"The accusative marks the direct object: *Vidím ženu.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The accusative marks the direct object, the person or thing a verb acts on. It also follows *pre* (for) and *na* when it means *onto* or *to*.\n\n- Feminine nouns in *-a* take *-u*: *žena → ženu*, *ulica → ulicu*, *gazdiná → gazdinú*. Feminine nouns ending in a consonant do not change: *kosť*, *miestnosť*.\n- Masculine animate nouns take *-a*: *brat → brata*. Those in *-a* take *-u*: *hrdina → hrdinu*.\n- Masculine inanimate and neuter nouns look like the nominative: *Vidím dom. Vidím mesto.*","examples":[{"sk":"Vidím ženu.","en":"I see a woman.","highlight":{"start":6,"end":10}},{"sk":"Mám brata.","en":"I have a brother.","highlight":{"start":4,"end":9}},{"sk":"Idem na námestie.","en":"I am going to the square.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":16}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["verb-vidiet","prep-pre","prep-na-acc","q-koho-acc","q-co-acc"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"comprehension","content":{"kind":"comprehension","exerciseIds":["ex-140da36a9f","ex-41e52bdfd9","ex-95b51f9ebd","ex-4f4a53a75b","ex-23c3375a79","ex-4a17f20e77","ex-5c2e81b7a4","ex-5adbce8449","ex-d6ef446a27","ex-9dd0925067","ex-c3fbd5b283","ex-0163aff340"]}},{"ord":3,"kind":"production","content":{"kind":"production","exerciseIds":["ex-3b2e072c21","ex-04f2286efe","ex-9308112f39","ex-5a9a0b1564","ex-60c412ebd9","ex-b8c82eb2c4","ex-3fa94c21d0","ex-4fffb3db0d","ex-d83571bdf1","ex-c9b6517502","ex-23c01ee7c9","ex-23871d6f92"]}},{"ord":4,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-b84236ccfd","ex-57f44308d5","ex-71a40f9b6e","ex-9fe9bda7fe","ex-15a5a8b103","ex-09709d4f16","ex-4834c11990","ex-58164cd763","ex-323958b3bd"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"loc-sg","course":"declension","ord":2,"titleEn":"Locative singular","titleSk":"Lokál jednotného čísla","case":"loc","number":"sg","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"loc","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.3},{"case":"loc","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.3},{"case":"loc","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.25},{"case":"loc","number":"sg","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.15}],"triggerIds":["prep-v-loc","prep-na-loc","prep-o-loc","prep-pri","prep-po-loc","q-kde"]},"summaryMd":"The locative follows *v*, *na*, *o*, *pri* and *po*: *Bývam v Bratislave.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The locative appears only after a preposition. With *v* and *na* it says where something is, *o* means *about*, *pri* means *by* and *po* means *after*.\n\n- Hard masculine and neuter nouns take *-e*: *dom → v dome*, *mesto → v meste*. Soft ones take *-i*: *stroj → v stroji*, *srdce → v srdci*.\n- Masculine animate nouns take *-ovi*: *o bratovi*, *o hrdinovi*.\n- Feminine nouns in *-a* take *-e* after a hard consonant and *-i* after a soft one: *v Bratislave*, *na ulici*. Nouns in a consonant take *-i*: *v miestnosti*.","examples":[{"sk":"Bývam v Bratislave.","en":"I live in Bratislava.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":18}},{"sk":"Som v obchode.","en":"I am in the shop.","highlight":{"start":6,"end":13}},{"sk":"Hovoríme o bratovi.","en":"We are talking about my brother.","highlight":{"start":11,"end":18}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["prep-v-loc","prep-na-loc","prep-o-loc","prep-pri","prep-po-loc","q-kde"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"comprehension","content":{"kind":"comprehension","exerciseIds":["ex-68e8bd9c74","ex-c37ce2b216","ex-a44f8812e6","ex-e489b5d319","ex-866980bf47","ex-e7b965d8f9","ex-e7cb0b0740","ex-2319f36df6","ex-8e601cd8bd","ex-9d04b3e2f1","ex-0cfe45d9b1","ex-9730dd356e"]}},{"ord":3,"kind":"production","content":{"kind":"production","exerciseIds":["ex-897759c048","ex-3e0c6afbb6","ex-17e659c946","ex-6e5c2d9e03","ex-d3ff11cf4d","ex-9c2b2a61ce","ex-17c41dedd5","ex-0f310ea0e4","ex-fb7de462fd","ex-f69de86124","ex-02cadee4ca","ex-fa61d5a378"]}},{"ord":4,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-338473d9f9","ex-2211e305f2","ex-71064a54bc","ex-ac838a8842","ex-5ec9eb74c3","ex-35c3c382da","ex-4cd5c04b9e","ex-e0cc2504a1","ex-4f4e2caeb4"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"gen-sg","course":"declension","ord":3,"titleEn":"Genitive singular","titleSk":"Genitív jednotného čísla","case":"gen","number":"sg","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"gen","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.3},{"case":"gen","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.25},{"case":"gen","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.25},{"case":"gen","number":"sg","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.2}],"triggerIds":["prep-do","prep-z","prep-od","prep-bez"]},"summaryMd":"The genitive follows *do*, *z*, *od* and *bez*: *Idem do mesta.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The genitive follows *do* (to), *z* (from), *od* (from a person) and *bez* (without). Feminine nouns take *-y* or *-e*: *z Bratislavy*, *bez práce*. Neuter nouns take *-a*: *do mesta*.","examples":[{"sk":"Idem do mesta.","en":"I am going to town.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":13}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["prep-do","prep-z","prep-od","prep-bez"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-7b21c0d4e9","ex-8fcdc7697a","ex-9aaafb3eff","ex-56470a64a2"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"ins-sg","course":"declension","ord":4,"titleEn":"Instrumental singular","titleSk":"Inštrumentál jednotného čísla","case":"ins","number":"sg","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"ins","number":"sg","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.3},{"case":"ins","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.3},{"case":"ins","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.2},{"case":"ins","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.2}],"triggerIds":["prep-s-ins","q-s-kym"]},"summaryMd":"The instrumental follows *s* meaning *with*: *s kamarátom.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The instrumental follows *s* (with). Masculine and neuter nouns take *-om*: *s kamarátom*. Feminine nouns take *-ou*: *s prácou*.","examples":[{"sk":"Idem do kina s kamarátom.","en":"I am going to the cinema with a friend.","highlight":{"start":15,"end":24}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["prep-s-ins","q-s-kym"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-02a5298a45","ex-b11775c35b","ex-21081d7910"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"dat-pron","course":"declension","ord":5,"titleEn":"Dative, starting with pronouns","titleSk":"Datív, najprv zámená","case":"dat","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"dat","number":"sg","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.5},{"case":"dat","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.3},{"case":"dat","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.1},{"case":"dat","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.1}],"triggerIds":["verb-pomahat","prep-k","q-komu"]},"summaryMd":"The dative marks the person you help or go to: *Pomáham mu.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The dative marks the person something is done for. *Pomáhať* (to help) takes the dative, and so does *k* (towards). Start with the pronouns *mu* (him) and *jej* (her), then nouns: *Pomáham bratovi.*","examples":[{"sk":"Pomáham bratovi.","en":"I help my brother.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":15}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["verb-pomahat","prep-k","q-komu"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-b4e1f09a37","ex-16008b5771","ex-b95deb20d2","ex-5a10fe11fe"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"nom-acc-pl","course":"declension","ord":6,"titleEn":"Nominative and accusative plural","titleSk":"Nominatív a akuzatív množného čísla","number":"pl","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"nom","number":"pl","gender":"f","weight":0.25},{"case":"nom","number":"pl","gender":"n","weight":0.25},{"case":"acc","number":"pl","gender":"f","weight":0.25},{"case":"acc","number":"pl","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.25}],"triggerIds":["verb-vidiet"]},"summaryMd":"The plural of the subject and the object: *Mám dve knihy.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"In the plural, inanimate nouns have the same form in the nominative and the accusative: *knihy*, *domy*, *dievčatá*. Animate masculine nouns take the genitive form in the accusative.","examples":[{"sk":"Mám dve knihy.","en":"I have two books.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":13}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["verb-vidiet"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-71cea985fd","ex-28bc300481","ex-5c2676c1ec"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"loc-ins-dat-pl","course":"declension","ord":7,"titleEn":"Locative, instrumental and dative plural","titleSk":"Lokál, inštrumentál a datív množného čísla","number":"pl","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"loc","number":"pl","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.35},{"case":"ins","number":"pl","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.35},{"case":"dat","number":"pl","gender":"m_anim","weight":0.3}],"triggerIds":["prep-o-loc","prep-s-ins","verb-pomahat"]},"summaryMd":"Plural endings after prepositions and verbs: *o ľuďoch, s kamarátmi, rodičom.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"The plural locative ends in *-och* or *-ách*, the instrumental in *-mi* or *-ami*, and the dative in *-om* or *-ám*: *o ľuďoch*, *s kamarátmi*, *Pomáham rodičom.*","examples":[{"sk":"Hovoríme o ľuďoch.","en":"We are talking about people.","highlight":{"start":11,"end":17}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["prep-o-loc","prep-s-ins","verb-pomahat"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-1e3e3bb28a","ex-2b721a22c9","ex-233e14c7d6"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"gen-pl","course":"declension","ord":8,"titleEn":"Genitive plural","titleSk":"Genitív množného čísla","case":"gen","number":"pl","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"gen","number":"pl","gender":"f","weight":0.4},{"case":"gen","number":"pl","gender":"n","weight":0.3},{"case":"gen","number":"pl","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.3}],"triggerIds":["num-pat"]},"summaryMd":"After *päť* the noun is in the genitive plural: *päť kníh.*","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"After *päť* and higher numbers the noun is in the genitive plural. Feminine and neuter nouns often lose their ending and lengthen a vowel: *kníh*, *miest*. Masculine nouns take *-ov*: *päť počítačov*.","examples":[{"sk":"Mám päť kníh.","en":"I have five books.","highlight":{"start":8,"end":12}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["num-pat"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-e8ebfdec49","ex-38617e73f0","ex-4aa6cdf8c8"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
{"id":"mixed","course":"declension","ord":9,"titleEn":"All cases together","titleSk":"Všetky pády","focus":{"buckets":[{"case":"gen","number":"sg","gender":"m_inan","weight":0.3},{"case":"loc","number":"sg","gender":"n","weight":0.3},{"case":"acc","number":"sg","gender":"f","weight":0.4}],"triggerIds":["prep-z","prep-pri","prep-pre"]},"summaryMd":"Every case together, chosen by the word before the gap.","prerequisites":[],"steps":[{"ord":0,"kind":"explain","content":{"kind":"explain","md":"Every case together. Look at the word before the gap: the preposition or the verb chooses the case.","examples":[{"sk":"Kúpil som kávu pre ženu.","en":"I bought coffee for my wife.","highlight":{"start":19,"end":23}}]}},{"ord":1,"kind":"triggers","content":{"kind":"triggers","triggerIds":["prep-z","prep-pri","prep-pre"]}},{"ord":2,"kind":"checkpoint","content":{"kind":"checkpoint","exerciseIds":["ex-4f360c2cdb","ex-559cd71382","ex-3e3e34a68b"],"passShare":0.75}}]}
